{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/739094-blood-potency-6-and-the-embrace","id":739094,"title":"Blood Potency 6 and the embrace.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-29T11:40:14-07:00","id":739094,"title":"Blood Potency 6 and the embrace.","content":"Is a blood potency 6 char probaly going to rely on &quot;Embracing the Dead&quot; since she cant hold down mortal blood or have someone else drain the person first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T11:53:01-07:00","id":739186,"title":"","content":"They can hold down mortal blood just fine. It just doesn't turn into vitae without effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:19:04-07:00","id":739264,"title":"","content":"It's always been my impression that blood potency 6 vampires rely on political capital and maneuvering to feed their hunger. The necessity of building relationships that can sustain elders as they grow more powerful strikes me as one of the major reasons these otherwise solitary predators gather into communities. Territory and political sway allows them to establish relationships of serfdom and symbiosis that provides them with, essentially, a herd of kindred. Even then, sinking into torpor to eliminate those hassles is a pretty prevalent choice among elders.<br /> <br /> I like the structure. It creates a neat risk/reward mechanic between your inherent power and the responsibilities involved with that power, and it encourages characters to pursue relationships within the local community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:25:03-07:00","id":739283,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but this isn't about hunger. This is about draining a human of blood as a prerequisite for embrace. <i>That </i>they can do just fine. It's like how using protean to change into an animal requires finding an example of what you want to take the form of and completely draining it. You can still do that at potency 3 and up, despite the blood no longer nourishing you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:38:31-07:00","id":739304,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm not saying they can't do that mechanically. It just doesn't strike me as a sustainable survival method.<br /> <br /> Acts of premeditated and prolific murder executed to create a herd of undead bloodcattle is going to tear your humanity to shreds with alarming quickness.<br /> <br /> Even if that weren't the case, it's going to draw a lot of muscle down from hunters and kindred unless you're real good at covering your tracks.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oops, I think I misinterpreted the question. Sorry guys! I totally veered off track. Elfive's totally on the money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-29-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:45:51-07:00","id":741738,"title":"","content":"I would think that they would drain the person dry themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:54:27-07:00","id":741754,"title":"","content":"Or they can simply hook the prospective childe up to a blood salvage or hemodialysis machine and exsanguinate them that way, make the pre-requisite vitae, willpower, humanity sacrifice and feed their newly embraced childe the same blood they just drained from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:06:49-07:00","id":741795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/739094-blood-potency-6-and-the-embrace?p=739264#post739264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always been my impression that blood potency 6 vampires rely on political capital and maneuvering to feed their hunger. The necessity of building relationships that can sustain elders as they grow more powerful strikes me as one of the major reasons these otherwise solitary predators gather into communities. Territory and political sway allows them to establish relationships of serfdom and symbiosis that provides them with, essentially, a herd of kindred. Even then, sinking into torpor to eliminate those hassles is a pretty prevalent choice among elders.<br /> <br /> I like the structure. It creates a neat risk/reward mechanic between your inherent power and the responsibilities involved with that power, and it encourages characters to pursue relationships within the local community.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or to just become powerful enough that they DGAF. Like the <i>only </i>vampire my Hunter/Sin-Eater is actually afraid of...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}